## 25.11 Embedding association and representation bias

Embedding models represent words, sentences, or documents as vectors.  Bias can appear as geometric association.  Let $X$ and $Y$ be two sets of target words, and let $A$ and $B$ be two sets of attribute words.  A simple association score is

$$
s(w,A,B)=\frac{1}{|A|}\sum_{a\in A}\cos(e_w,e_a)
-
\frac{1}{|B|}\sum_{b\in B}\cos(e_w,e_b).
$$

A set-level effect score is

$$
S(X,Y,A,B)=\sum_{x\in X}s(x,A,B)-\sum_{y\in Y}s(y,A,B).
$$

This type of score is inspired by word-embedding association tests and related representation-auditing methods @caliskan_semantics_2017, @bolukbasi_man_is_2016.

::: {.cell execution_count=7}
